From 7adbffc0138dda8f8021abb5ba12e3b12681a02b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 20:21:55 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 26/29] net: import the minimal TCP stack and DHCP server for
 the rescue page

Import the GPL-2.0 U-Boot TCP stack and the tiny DHCP server from
bl-mt798x-dhcpd (master e4cf4dc72d451dc7a86c9508390ad5a2e50743c4)
so that the E2631 web rescue can serve its own page, without any
host-side network stack and without an external HTTP server.

The files are taken from that tree, with these deliberate changes:

  - mtk_tcp.c includes the private net/mtk_tcp_priv.h instead of the
    public header, so that the frame/state definitions stay local to net/;
  - the public include/net/mtk_tcp.h carries the API and also declares
    mtk_receive_tcp(), which net/net.c uses below;
  - net/mtk_dhcpd.c drops the upstream "dhcpd" console command; only the
    start/stop/is_running API is kept, since the rescue owns the pool;
  - net/net.c gains a CONFIG_MTK_TCP hook in the IPv4 path that hands TCP
    frames to mtk_receive_tcp() instead of a listener. It is guarded by
    the new symbol, so the default build is unchanged;
  - arp_wait_clear() is added, because the stack clears a completed ARP
    wait before sending into an unknown neighbour and U-Boot only had
    arp_is_waiting().

CONFIG_MTK_TCP and CONFIG_MTK_DHCPD are new, off by default; the E2631
defconfig turns them on in the final patch of this series. While they are
off no code from this commit is built.

Signed-off-by: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
